{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1793392000000-architect-adopt-signoff.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n cat collab/1793393000000-engineer-adopt-fix4.prompt.md\n rg -n '45269e0f|12feb7d1|shiva' orchestrator-logs collab -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-30 20:12:43 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-31 03:12:43 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nSIGN-OFF: denied. Scope: `63674368..12feb7d1` on `yang-common-call`. One required change remains.\n\n**P2 — The invocation admission gate skips argument evaluation on refusal.** In [clojure.cljc:1305](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yang-common-call/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1305), positional, named, and options operands are evaluated only in the admitted branch. This violates §8.10.4’s source evaluation requirements.\n\nUsing the existing profile-raise harness, I independently probed:\n\n```clojure\n(yang.call/invoke\n  5 (probe/note [21]) (probe/note []) profile-raise)\n\n(yang.call/invoke-with\n  5 (probe/note [21]) (probe/note []) profile-raise\n  (probe/note {}))\n```\n\nAt parent `abbfb998`, these record `[21]`, `[]`, and—where supplied—`{}` before the refusal. At `12feb7d1`, **none of those argument effects occur**; only the refusal is recorded. Confirmed on both walker and semantic lanes.\n\nRequired fix: evaluate and bind all operands exactly once, left to right, before the witness check; use those bindings in both branches. Add regressions covering refused callees through both operators, including options evaluation.\n\nThe prior admission and manifest findings are otherwise addressed. The reported source-spelled raise limitation remains non-blocking under the existing ruling.\n\nAfter correction, refresh verification at the final commit. Node/Dart completion and the repository’s required `dao.stream` gate remain merge conditions. No tracked files were changed during this review.Created-GMT: 2026-10-30 20:15:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-31 03:15:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: kimi\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: adopt-fix4-operand-order\nRole: Compiler & AST Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: kimi-code/k3.1-pro | Assigned: 2026-10-31 03:15:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: bounded fix; codex astra authored the finding.\n\nWork in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yang-common-call (branch yang-common-call @12feb7d1). Files: src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc and test/yang/clojure_test.clj only.\n\nArchitect (astra) finding on the N1 fix — P2: THE INVOCATION ADMISSION GATE SKIPS ARGUMENT EVALUATION ON REFUSAL.\nAt src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1305 the positional, named and options operands are evaluated only in the ADMITTED branch of the new yang.call/invoke + invoke-with admission gate. §8.10.4 requires source operands to evaluate exactly once, in source order, before the callee is entered (and refusals must not suppress those effects).\n\nProbe (astra's, using the existing profile-raise harness):\n  (yang.call/invoke 5 (probe/note [21]) (probe/note []) profile-raise)\n  (yang.call/invoke-with 5 (probe/note [21]) (probe/note []) profile-raise (probe/note {}))\nAt parent abbfb998 these record [21], [] and {} BEFORE the refusal. At 12feb7d1 none of the argument effects occur — only the refusal. Confirmed on both walker and semantic lanes.\n\nFIX: evaluate and bind ALL operands exactly once, left to right, BEFORE the witness check, and use those bindings in BOTH the admitted and refused branches. Do not duplicate evaluation (no re-evaluating operands in the admitted arm). Same discipline as the compiler already applies elsewhere (see how other multi-operand forms bind temps once).\n\nRegressions: refused callees through BOTH operators must still run their argument effects, in order, exactly once — including the options operand for invoke-with. Add positive-path controls that admitted calls still evaluate once in order. Cover both lanes.\n\nVerify: clj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yang.core.call-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n dao.host.gate-test -> 0 failures; oracle corpus (yang.latte-oracle-test) unchanged at 21/971 (its one intentional gate failure expected); kondo 0 errors, no new warnings. Commit on yang-common-call (format.md). Do not push.\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:96:  verification goes to shiva/jupiter (build-n-test.md's laptop-unload rule) or waits. The kimi\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:107:  (my killed local run) moves into the S1 engineering brief on shiva.\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:109:  codex in the isolated checkout, with verification on shiva; the wiring slices stay gated on the\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:112:## 2026-10-30 09:3x +07 — S1 round landed on its branch; the in-slice rule caught a false claim; the baseline captured on shiva\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:122:  deferred restored; committed d2b3224a; the slow scan test green (12/716/0). The report's shiva\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:123:  baseline failed on its sandbox DNS; I captured the BEFORE baseline myself on a fresh shiva clone\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:138:  later acceptance work). The AFTER-state lanes on shiva at d2b3224a: lower-portable 5/19/0,\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:14:Done: Re-derived state per claude's handoff (all claims verified: worktree diff 3 files, fable stdout empty -> dispatch lost). Re-dispatched the architect decision to fable (session 8c1f0b7e resumed, collab/1793190906382-architect-yang-slice3-multiarity.*): verdict — destructuring/headers SIGNED OFF as-is (kondo baseline condition); multi-arity SPLIT to slice 3b on the argument-vector convention with corpus evidence (14 multi-arity LaTTe fns; type-of shifts positions so nil-fill fails) and a hard no-yin-files rule; first/rest/empty? departure RATIFIED (plan's nth unsoun