{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2010,2120p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n sed -n '920,1310p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj\n git diff 63674368..45269e0f -- docs test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"                                                         (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n       (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                           'dsg__admitted?\n                           (u/sexp->uast\n                             '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n                                  (let [dsg__entry (dsg__get dsg__candidate :yang.call/entry)\n                                        dsg__witness (dsg__get dsg__candidate :clj/admission)]\n                                    (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n                                      (dsg__equal\n                                        dsg__witness\n                                        (dsg__make_admission\n                                          (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate :clj/admission nil)))\n                                      false))\n                                  false))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                           'dsg__make_admission\n                           (u/sexp->uast\n                             '(fn [dsg__descriptor]\n                                (fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                  (if (data/callable? dsg__call_token)\n                                    (dsg__get dsg__descriptor :yang.call/entry)\n                                    nil)))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/then\n                           (discard-result\n                             (u/app (u/lam '[get = assoc empty?] call/uast)\n                                    (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                    (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v 'dsg__empty))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__call_token (u/lam [] (u/lit nil)))\n         ;; Guest closures keep captured environments portable: binding host\n         ;; primitive values here would make UCF machine-data validation fail.\n         ;; These helpers cover generated map lookups/writes and comparisons;\n         ;; conj/vec are already protected by the convention's binder checks.\n         ;; Evaluate siblings outside each other's bindings to avoid retaining\n         ;; a chain of redundant helper environments.\n         (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                             (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n                             (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 '(fn [m k]\n                                    (if (data/map? m)\n                                      (let [find (fn [self entries]\n                                                   (if (data/content= 0 (data/count entries))\n                                                     nil\n                                                     (let [pair (data/nth entries 0)]\n                                                       (if (data/content= k (data/nth pair 0))\n                                                         (data/nth pair 1)\n                                                         (self self (data/subvec entries 1))))))]\n                                        (find find (vec m)))\n                                      nil)))\n                               (u/sexp->uast '(fn [m k] (get m k))))\n                             (u/sexp->uast '(fn [a b] (data/content= a b)))\n                             (u/sexp->uast\n                               '(fn [m k v k2 v2 k3 v3]\n                                  (let [one (conj m (conj [] k v))]\n                                    (if (data/content= k2 nil)\n                                      one\n                                      (let [two (conj one (conj [] k2 v2))]\n                                        (if (data/content= k3 nil)\n                                          two\n                                          (conj two (conj [] k3 v3))))))))\n                             (u/sexp->uast '(fn [xs] (data/content= 0 (data/count xs))))))\n         (outcomes? env) u/mark-tails)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The guest collection and higher-order library (slice 7)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Guest-side source, compiled through this compiler like any program: the\n;; functions that invoke guest closures (map, filter, reduce, comp, partial)\n;; must run on the VM, never on the host, because a closure is a VM value. It\n;; is written for the argument-vector convention with the outcome model, so a\n;; closure it calls is unwrapped by the compiler's own early-return pattern\n;; and a closure's failure ends the library function with the same outcome.\n;;\n;; What is derived, from the VM primitives and the `data` module only:\n;; identity, inc/dec, second, the collection predicates (coll?/vector?/map?/\n;; set?/seq?/list?/sequential?, from the `portable/*` adapters of data/count,\n;; peek, dissoc and disj: a refusal as data says \"not that kind\"), boolean?,\n;; fn? (data/callable?), seq, rem, reverse, list, cons, vector, count,\n;; contains?, rest, map/mapv/filter/remove/reduce (with reduced)/into/concat/merge,\n;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\n;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\n;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\n;;\n;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\n;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\n;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\n;; (meta). No `data` export or\n;; VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. var? and resolve are the host's\n;; Var primitives: a harness on a host with Vars registers them in `kind`\n;; (`kind-module` leaves them out); a program that never mentions them does\n;; not need them.\n;;\n;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\n;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\n;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\n;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\n;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\n;;\n;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\n;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\n;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\n;; A larger count is the\n;; function's own arity error.\n\n(def library-adapters\n  (testing \"top-level definitions are unaffected, and the native path is unchanged\"\n    (is (not (rejected-av? '[(def a 1) (defn f\n                                         []\n                                         a) (f)])))\n    (is (= 1 (run-native '[(do (def a 1)) a])))))\n\n\n(deftest test-defmacro-param-checks\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [dsg__x]\n                    1)))\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [[a b]]\n                    1)))\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [& a b]\n                    1)))\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [&]\n                    1)))\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [a & b & c]\n                    1)))\n  (is (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                    [:k]\n                    1)))\n  (is (not (rejected? '(defmacro m\n                         [a & b]\n                         1))))\n  (is (not (rejected? '(defmacro defn\n                         [& xs]\n                         1)))))\n\n\n;; --- tail-position audit -----------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- ast-nodes\n  [ast]\n  (tree-seq coll? #(if (map? %) (vals %) (seq %)) ast))\n\n\n(defn- applications\n  \"[operator-name-or-:lambda tail?] of every application node.\"\n  [ast]\n  (->> (ast-nodes ast)\n       (filter #(and (map? %) (= :application (:type %))))\n       (map (fn [a]\n              [(if (= :variable (get-in a [:operator :type]))\n                 (get-in a [:operator :name])\n                 (get-in a [:operator :type]))\n               (boolean (:tail? a))]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-loop-tail-audit\n  (let [form '(loop [i 0] (if (< i 3) (recur (+ i 1)) i))]\n    (testing \"exactly the let chain, the initial application and the recur are tail\"\n      (is (= {[:lambda true] 2        ; initializer let, worker-binding let\n              ['dsg__loop0 true] 2    ; initial application, recur\n              ['< false] 1            ; the test\n              ['+ false] 1}           ; a recur operand is never tail\n             (frequencies (applications (yang/compile form))))))\n    (testing \"a loop in operand position is not itself tail; its recur still is\"\n      (is (= {[:lambda false] 2, ['dsg__loop0 false] 1, ['dsg__loop0 true] 1\n              ['< false] 1, ['+ false] 1}\n             (frequencies (applications (yang/compile-form form false {}))))))))\n\n\n;; --- continuation-depth gates -----------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- walker-depth\n  \"Length of the :next chain from the VM's k.\"\n  [vm]\n  (loop [k (vm/continuation vm), n 0]\n    (if k (recur (:next k) (inc n)) n)))\n\n\n(defn- semantic-depth\n  [vm]\n  (count (vm/continuation vm)))\n\n\n(defn- stepper\n  \"A run function stepping the VM one instruction at a time, recording the\n   maximum depth `depth-of` reports in :max-depth.\"\n  [depth-of]\n  (fn [vm]\n    (loop [v vm, mx (depth-of vm)]\n      (if (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v))\n        (assoc v :max-depth mx)\n        (let [v' (vm/step v)]\n          (recur v' (max mx (depth-of v'))))))))\n\n\n(defn- walker-run\n  \"[value max-depth] of `ast` on the walker lane.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [session (-> (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules av-modules}))\n                    (tu/queue-ast! ast))\n        done (observer/run-on-stream\n               session engine/ready-for-ingress?\n               (vm/fresh-code-loader ast-walker/vm-load-program vm/ast-contract)\n               (stepper walker-depth))]\n    [(vm/value (:consumer done)) (:max-depth (:consumer done))]))\n\n\n(defn- semantic-run\n  \"[value max-depth] of `ast` on the semantic lane.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [session (tu/make-encoder-session\n                  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                       :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                       :modules av-modules}))\n        load-rows (vm/fresh-code-loader\n                    (fn [machine rows stamp]\n                      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n                      (semantic/load-vector\n                        machine\n                        (:vector (if (contains? rows :yin/batch)\n                                   (linearize/project-rows\n                                     (nth (:yin/batch rows) (:yin/root rows))\n                                     (vm/source-origin (:yin/source-medium rows)\n                                                       (:yin/batch-token rows)\n                                                       (:yin/root rows)))\n                                   (linearize/project-rows rows)))\n                        vm/semantic-contract))\n                    vm/ast-contract)]\n    (stream/append! (:program session) ast)\n    (let [encoded (assoc session :encoder (encoder/forward-on-stream (:encoder session)))\n          done (observer/run-on-stream (:evaluator encoded) engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                       load-rows (stepper semantic-depth))]\n      [(vm/value (:consumer done)) (:max-depth (:consumer done))])))\n\n\n(defn- countdown-ast\n  \"A program counting down from n through a loop or a function-level recur,\n   in tail position or as an operand of conj.\"\n  [kind n shape]\n  (let [form (walk/postwalk-replace\n               {'N n}\n               (case kind\n                 :loop '(loop [i N] (if (= i 0) :done (recur (- i 1))))\n                 :fn '((fn [i] (if (= i 0) :done (recur (- i 1)))) N)))]\n    (yang/compile-program [(if (= shape :tail) form (list 'conj [] form))] true)))\n\n\n(defn- strip-self-tail\n  \"Remove :tail? from every application of a worker self name.\"\n  [ast]\n  (walk/postwalk\n    (fn [node]\n      (if (and (map? node)\n               (= :application (:type node))\n               (= :variable (get-in node [:operator :type]))\n               (re-find #\"^dsg__loop\" (str (get-in node [:operator :name]))))\n        (dissoc node :tail?)\n        node))\n    ast))\n\n\n(deftest test-continuation-depth-gates\n  (doseq [[lane run-lane] [[:walker walker-run] [:semantic semantic-run]]\n          kind [:loop :fn]\n          shape [:tail :operand]]\n    (let [run (fn [n] (run-lane (countdown-ast kind n shape)))\n          [_ d0] (run 0)\n          [v100 d100] (run 100)\n          [v1000 d1000] (run 1000)\n          label (str lane \" \" kind \" \" shape)]\n      (is (= (if (= shape :tail) :done [:done]) v100 v1000) label)\n      (is (= d100 d1000) (str label \": depth is constant in the iteration count\"))\n      (when (= lane :semantic)\n        (is (<= d1000 (+ d0 2)) (str label \": at most 2 above the pre-loop depth\")))))\n  ;; The walker lane masks a missing flag (its depth stays flat either way),\n  ;; so only the semantic lane can serve as the flag-sensitive control.\n  (testing \"negative control: without :tail? on the self-application depth grows\"\n    (let [run (fn [n] (semantic-run (strip-self-tail (countdown-ast :loop n :tail))))\n          [_ d0] (run 0)\n          [_ d100] (run 100)]\n      (is (> d100 (+ d0 50)) \"the semantic gate detects the missing flag\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Slice 5: the outcome model\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private effect-log (atom []))\n\n\n(def ^:private outcome-modules\n  (let [host (fn [name entries]\n               (fn [registry]\n                 (module/register-host-module\n                   registry name\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op f _]] [op f])) entries)\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op _ p]] [op p])) entries))))]\n    (-> av-modules\n        ((host 'portable\n               [['nth\n                 (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message (get data/data-module 'nth))\n                 (get data/data-profiles 'nth)]]))\n        ((host 'probe\n               [['note\n                 (fn [x] (swap! effect-log conj x) x)\n                 (vm/primitive-profile 'note :pure [1] #{} :none)]])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private outcome-opts\n  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n   :native (set (keys vm/primitives))\n   :adapters {'data/nth 'portable/nth}})\n\n\n(defn- outcome-ast\n  [forms]\n  (yang/compile-program forms true outcome-opts))\n\n\n(defn- run-outcome\n  \"The raw outcome the last form of `forms` returns.\"\n  [forms]\n  (reset! effect-log [])\n  (-> (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules outcome-modules}))\n      (tu/queue-ast! (outcome-ast forms))\n      tu/run-session\n      :consumer\n      vm/value))\n\n\n(defn- run-profile-outcome\n  [forms]\n  (reset! effect-log [])\n  (let [ast (walk/postwalk\n              (fn [node]\n                (if (= node (u/v 'profile-raise)) (u/v 'probe/note) node))\n              (outcome-ast forms))]\n    (-> (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules outcome-modules}))\n        (tu/queue-ast! ast)\n        tu/run-session\n        :consumer\n        vm/value)))\n\n\n(deftest test-outcome-success-and-throw\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok 2] (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                                        [x]\n                                        (+ x 1)) (f 1)])))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok [:ok 1]] (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                                              [x]\n                                              [:ok x]) (f 1)]))\n      \"LaTTe's own [:ok ...] stays an ordinary value inside the payload\")\n  (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"boom\", :yin.k/data {:x 1}}]\n         (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                          [x]\n                          (throw (ex-info \"boom\" {:x x}))) (f 1)])))\n  (testing \"an untaken throw branch leaves the success outcome\"\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :survived]\n           (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                            [x]\n                            (if x (throw (ex-info \"t\" {})) :survived))\n                          (f false)])))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-descriptor-publication\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok [:function true 2 3]]\n         (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                          [x]\n                          (+ x 1))\n                        [(get f :clj/type)\n                         (data/callable? (yang.call/entry f))\n                         (f 1)\n                         (let [plain +] (plain 1 2))]])))\n  (testing \"condition-shaped return data is still a successful value\"\n    (let [value {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                 :yang.call/value :ordinary-data}]\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok value]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'defn 'f [] value) '(f)]))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-hand-constructed-descriptor\n  (testing \"explicit UAST/profile construction admits a foreign body\"\n    ;; The constructor runs inside the compiled profile's private bindings.\n    ;; No Clojure source map receives admission from its entry spelling.\n    (let [descriptor (#'yang/admit-call-descriptor\n                      (u/sexp->uast\n                        '(assoc {} :foreign/type :function\n                                :yang.call/entry\n                                (fn [record] (get record :yang.call/positional))))\n                      false)]\n      (doseq [[form expected] [['(profile-function 40 2) [:yin.k/ok [40 2]]]\n                               ['[(profile-function 40 2)] [:yin.k/ok [[40 2]]]]]\n              run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n        (let [ast (walk/postwalk\n                    (fn [node]\n                      (if (= node (u/v 'profile-function)) descriptor node))\n                    (outcome-ast [form]))]\n          (is (= expected (first (run ast)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-profile-eligibility\n  (doseq [eligible? [true false]\n          run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n    (let [descriptor (#'yang/admit-call-descriptor\n                      (u/app (u/v 'assoc) (u/lit {})\n                             (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/lam ['record] (u/lit :called))\n                             (u/lit :yang.call/eligible?) (u/lam ['callee] (u/lit eligible?)))\n                      false)\n          profile-ast (fn [form]\n                        (walk/postwalk\n                          (fn [node]\n                            (cond (= node (u/v 'profile-function)) descriptor\n                                  (= node (u/v 'profile-raise)) (u/lam ['condition]\n                                                                      (u/v 'condition))\n                                  :else node))\n                          (outcome-ast [form])))]\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok eligible?]\n             (first (run (profile-ast '(yang.call/eligible? profile-function))))))\n      (doseq [form '[(profile-function)\n                     (yang.call/invoke profile-function [] [] profile-raise)\n                     (yang.call/invoke-with profile-function [] [] profile-raise {})]]\n        (let [result (first (run (profile-ast form)))]\n          (if eligible?\n            (is (= [:yin.k/ok :called] result))\n            (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason (second result))))))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-invocation-source-admission\n  (doseq [invoke-form '[(yang.call/invoke h [21] [] profile-raise)\n                        (yang.call/invoke-with h [21] [] profile-raise {})]\n          entry-form '[(get f :yang.call/entry) 5 (fn [invocation] :forged)]]\n    (let [forged (list 'assoc {} :yang.call/entry entry-form)\n          result (run-profile-outcome\n                   ['(defn f\n                       [x]\n                       (+ x 21))\n                    (list 'let ['h forged]\n                          (list 'get invoke-form :yang.call/reason))])]\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable] result)\n          (pr-str invoke-form))))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok [42 42]]\n         (run-profile-outcome\n           '[(defn f\n               [x]\n               (+ x 21))\n             [(yang.call/invoke f [21] [] profile-raise)\n              (yang.call/invoke-with f [21] [] profile-raise {})]]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-invocation-operand-order\n  (with-redefs [av-modules outcome-modules]\n    (doseq [run [walker-run semantic-run]\n            [operator options expected] '[[yang.call/invoke nil [[21] []]]\n                                          [yang.call/invoke-with {} [[21] [] {}]]]]\n      (doseq [admitted? [false true]]\n        (let [callee (if admitted? 'f 5)\n              invoke (if options\n                       (list operator callee '(probe/note [21]) '(probe/note [])\n                             'profile-raise (list 'probe/note options))\n                       (list operator callee '(probe/note [21]) '(probe/note [])\n                             'profile-raise))\n              ast (walk/postwalk\n                    (fn [node]\n                      (if (= node (u/v 'profile-raise))\n                        (u/lam ['condition] (u/lit :refused))\n                        node))\n                    (outcome-ast (if admitted?\n                                   ['(defn f [x] (+ x 21)) invoke]\n                                   [invoke])))\n              _ (reset! effect-log [])\n              [result] (run ast)]\n          (is (= expected @effect-log) (str operator \" admitted=\" admitted?))\n          (when admitted?\n            (is (= [:yin.k/ok 42] result) (str operator))))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-shadowed-helpers\n  (doseq [binding '[get = assoc empty?]]\n    (testing (str \"construction and invocation with a local \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 21]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'let [binding 5]\n                                 '(let [f (fn [x] x)] (f 21)))]))))\n    (testing (str \"a later source definition of \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 21]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'def binding 5) '(defn f\n                                                    [x]\n                                                    x) '(f 21)]))))\n    (testing (str \"raise through a parameter named \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"boom\", :yin.k/data {:x 21}}]\n             (run-outcome\n               ['(defn g\n                   []\n                   (throw (ex-info \"boom\" {:x 21})))\ndiff --git a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\nindex 3b6838e1..8df4069f 100644\n--- a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n+++ b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n@@ -176,3 +176,39 @@ reported zero errors/warnings; `cljstyle check` passed. The requested\n files. Linting an archived `1fe3eb07` baseline produced identical findings;\n those pre-existing Jolt/probe findings are outside this contract's file scope.\n | jolt ws: a ping after a local close is queued gets no pong (A4 \"every ping produces one pong\" holds until a local close exists) | pump.jolt:597 (handle-event! :ping guard); wave-1 Architect sign-off P3 | jolt (J6) | documented behaviour, closed by J6e's docstring sentences; J6h cites the archived sign-off | P3 |\n+\n+\n+## Clojure common-call arbitration dispositions (2026-10-30)\n+\n+Append-only disposition of Kimi r4. The two recorded deviations stand;\n+this entry does not alter or retire existing ledger rows.\n+\n++-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n+| Disposition                   | Evidence                                          | Construction / resolution                                                      |\n++===============================+===================================================+================================================================================+\n+| (a) source forgery: closed    | Kimi r4 arbitration, 1793309600000; test-common-  | A private factory creates a closure over the canonical descriptor and a        |\n+|                               | call-source-admission and explicit UAST/profile   | lexical token. Admission reconstructs and compares the opaque closure; it      |\n+|                               | fixture                                           | never calls a candidate hook. Copying the entry or changing descriptor fields  |\n+|                               |                                                   | fails. No VM type, descriptor seal, or provenance registry. Equal immutable    |\n+|                               |                                                   | reconstructions retain the same value.                                         |\n++-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n+| (d) constant stack: restored  | test-outcome-common-call-depth: named and mutual  | Every source callee is admitted before common invocation. Constructor entries  |\n+|                               | calls, walker and semantic lanes, 100/1000        | accept a private outcome option and tail-apply their private body, forwarding  |\n+|                               | iterations                                        | its outcome without pending conversion frames. Public/profile entries retain   |\n+|                               |                                                   | value/raise conversion. The non-tail negative control still grows.             |\n++-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n+\n+The same fix uses portable guest closures for the private get, equality,\n+assoc and empty aliases, refuses unadmitted source callees with the qualified\n+not-callable condition, and rejects invalid continuation captures explicitly.\n+A raise resumes only through the compiler's private transfer packet.\n+Nonempty named arguments still raise yang.call/thrown with the original\n+binding error payload, as required by arbitration (e).\n+\n+Verification: the four requested JVM namespaces plus the full accumulated\n+LaTTe oracle corpus pass together: 147 tests, 2,238 assertions, zero failures\n+or errors. This includes both 100/1,000 iteration depth lanes, their non-tail\n+negative control, the new rejection fixtures, and UCF reconstruction under\n+the existing validation and instruction budgets. Kondo reports zero errors\n+and the same two existing oracle-test warnings; formatting and whitespace\n+checks pass.\ndiff --git a/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn b/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\nindex 85e624c3..11e48635 100644\n--- a/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\n+++ b/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\n@@ -3,8 +3,8 @@\n {:lane :clj,\n  :root yin.repl.main,\n  :features #{:clj},\n- :total 155,\n- :shared 147,\n+ :total 156,\n+ :shared 148,