{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '45269e0f|12feb7d1' orchestrator-logs collab -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"collab/1793389000000-engineer-adopt-fix3.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md:4:  Implemented and committed N1/N2 as `12feb7d1` (`Gate yang.call invocation on admitted callees`).\ncollab/1793391000000-reviewer-adopt-n1n2.prompt.md:22:Fix commit: 12feb7d1 (git diff abbfb998..12feb7d1).\ncollab/1793393000000-engineer-adopt-fix4.prompt.md:11:Work in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yang-common-call (branch yang-common-call @12feb7d1). Files: src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc and test/yang/clojure_test.clj only.\ncollab/1793393000000-engineer-adopt-fix4.prompt.md:19:At parent abbfb998 these record [21], [] and {} BEFORE the refusal. At 12feb7d1 none of the argument effects occur — only the refusal. Confirmed on both walker and semantic lanes.\ncollab/1793391000000-reviewer-adopt-n1n2.glm-5.3.findings.md:4:Third confirmation round, narrowly scoped to the two P2s I raised in r2, against fix commit `12feb7d1` (`git diff abbfb998..12feb7d1`, re-read from the diff, not assumed). All probes re-ran read-only on the JVM lane through the test namespace's own runners (`run-outcome`, `run-profile-outcome`, `walker-run`, `semantic-run`, `outcome-ast`) plus `#'yang.clojure/admit-call-descriptor` for the eligibility arms; no source files edited, nothing committed. Probe-honesty note: my r2 report quoted the probes with a bare `raise` operand; this round established that source-spelled fn/defn values are descriptor **maps**, not applicable values, in this lane — the verdict-bearing probes below therefore spell raise exactly the way the corpus and the compiler's own bridges do (an applicable `probe/note` host splice / raw lam), and the source-spelled-raise behavior is reported separately as informational.\ncollab/1793391000000-reviewer-adopt-n1n2.glm-5.3.findings.md:38:**P3 | informational, pre-existing, non-blocking | source-spelled raise operands are not callable values.** `(fn [c] c)` or `(defn raise …)` in the raise operand compiles to a descriptor map (`compile-av-fn` → `compile-call-descriptor`, clojure.cljc:1116-1118); the shared runtime's `(if (data/callable? raise) … (raise …))` else-branch then applies the value it just decided is not callable (call.cljc:118,142) → host `{:reason :not-applicable, :kind :map}` \"Cannot apply non-function\". This crashes the **positive control identically** and `call.cljc` is byte-identical at `abbfb998`, so it is a pre-existing property of the surface (the invoke raise operand is profile-mediated: host fns and raw lams — the fixtures' `profile-raise` splices and the compiler's own bridges at clojure.cljc:1194,1234 — are the spellings that have ever worked), not a regression from `12feb7d1`; the new refusal path inherits the same class only for raise spellings that never worked anywhere on this surface. Recorded for the architect's list (the non-callable else-branch applying its own raise is the odd part); does not gate sign-off under r5, which pinned \"no change to `yang.core.call` is required\". Same class: under-arity `(yang.call/invoke h [21])` (below the branch's `(<= 4 …)` guard, pre-fix compilation unchanged) → host defect; over-arity tolerated (42) — both identical in class at the parent commit.\ncollab/1793391000000-reviewer-adopt-n1n2.glm-5.3.findings.md:69:**Ready for Architect sign-off.** Both P2s from r2 are closed with probe evidence at `12feb7d1`: the protocol's front door now refuses every unadmitted callee with the qualified `:yang.call/not-callable` condition through both operators (including the alias route), genuinely admitted callees — static and dynamic-eligibility — still work on both lanes, the shared runtime is untouched, and the closure gate test is green with the manifests regenerated. The one P3 (source-spelled raise operands being non-callable values, a pre-existing property that affects admitted callees identically and predates this fix) is recorded for the architect's backlog and does not gate this adoption.\ncollab/1793392000000-architect-adopt-signoff.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:4:SIGN-OFF: denied. Scope: `63674368..12feb7d1` on `yang-common-call`. One required change remains.\ncollab/1793392000000-architect-adopt-signoff.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:19:At parent `abbfb998`, these record `[21]`, `[]`, and—where supplied—`{}` before the refusal. At `12feb7d1`, **none of those argument effects occur**; only the refusal is recorded. Confirmed on both walker and semantic lanes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
