{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '625,646p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\n sed -n '270,310p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 shiva.stigmergy.systems 'ls -dt ~/ci/*call* ~/ci/*adopt* 2>/dev/null'\"","aggregated_output":"  finds route to fix rounds the next morning.\n- **Branch/worktree testing**: only the namespaces that target the\n  changed code (the diff's own tests plus the surfaces the diff touches),\n  one JVM per namespace, plus one cheap portable lane (Node) when cljc\n  goldens or fixtures moved. Never the full tier on a branch: a branch\n  gate needs the changed code proven, not the whole tree re-proven.\n\nAn orchestrator landing a slice cites the subset runs plus the gate\nsign-off; the nightly catches what the subset could not see, and a red\nnightly owns the follow-up.\n\n**The merge precondition (2026-10-30 owner ruling):** before any merge\ninto master, the `dao.stream` tests must run and pass — dao.stream is\nwhat everything is built on. Concretely: `bb test:sub dao.stream` (the\nsubsystem's tests, `--slow` when the slice touches slow-guarded\nsurfaces) is part of every branch gate regardless of which subsystems\nthe diff's own changes select, because a change can break the foundation\nwithout touching it. A red dao.stream blocks the merge until fixed or\ndiagnosed as pre-existing by the owning seat.\n\n### The nightly full suite and the branch-testing rule (2026-10-30 owner ruling)\n\n  \"qualified-fn | args for the A/C differential. The four anchors the\n   architect named first, plus leaf functions classified :clean.\"\n  {'latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv [[]]\n   'latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [[1 2 3 4] 2]})\n\n\n(defn- upstream-fn\n  [qsym]\n  (requiring-resolve qsym))\n\n\n(deftest test-oracle-classification\n  (testing \"every manifest entry has source\"\n    (is (every? (fn [{:keys [ns name]}] (get top-forms [ns name])) manifest)))\n  (testing \"architect anchor classifications (slice 1 narrowing table)\"\n    ;; utils/vconcat uses loop/recur\n    (is (contains? (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'vconcat]))\n                   :loop))\n    ;; utils/pair? is structurally simple but calls host fn `vector` and\n    ;; carries a docstring: both must be classified as blockers\n    (is (contains? (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'pair?]))\n                   'vector))\n    ;; syntax/alpha-norm is blocked by more than its docstring\n    (is (seq (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.syntax 'alpha-norm]))))\n    ;; nbe/norm is blocked\n    (is (seq (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.nbe 'norm])))))\n  (testing \"A/C differential on admitted fixtures\"\n    (let [results\n          (for [[qsym args] fixtures\n                :let [f (upstream-fn qsym)\n                      a-value (apply f args)\n                      fname (symbol (name qsym))\n                      c-result (try\n                                 {:status :ok\n                                  :value (run-on-vm\n                                           (cond-> (vec clean-forms)\n                                             (not (some #{fname} (map second clean-forms)))\n                                             (conj (get top-forms\n                                                        [(symbol (str/replace (namespace qsym) \"-\" \"_\"))\n                                                         fname])))\n                                           (list* fname args))}\nssh: Could not resolve hostname shiva.stigmergy.systems: nodename nor servname provided, or not known\r\n","exit_code":255,"status":"failed"}}
